WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.240
All right.

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:02.909
Let's get into audience questions for the
week.

00:00:02.909 --> 00:00:05.919
A lot of questions about the Supreme Court.

00:00:05.919 --> 00:00:10.940
Ruth Bader Ginsburg and one of those questions
I received from many people in the last few

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.980
days is whether Roe v. Wade is gone.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:20.789
If Donald Trump replaces Ruth Bader Ginsburg,
it does seem I mean, listen, we're going to

00:00:20.789 --> 00:00:26.010
see what happens, but it seems increasingly
likely that Donald Trump is going to be able

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:28.990
to fill that vacancy on the Supreme Court.

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:31.689
Whether they do it before Election Day.

00:00:31.689 --> 00:00:33.090
I don't know.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:39.470
But even if Joe Biden were to win on November
3rd, it does maybe even more so if Joe Biden

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:40.880
were to win on November 3rd.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:47.350
It does seem that there are going to be enough
votes from Republicans in the Senate.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:50.490
Remember, you need 51, Republicans have 53.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:54.860
And only two senators have said they would
wait at least until after the election.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:58.330
We don't we don't know if they would insist
on waiting until the inauguration.

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:00.390
It seems they're going to have 51.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:05.059
So one of the big questions is whether Roe
v. Wade, which is a landmark United States

00:01:05.059 --> 00:01:12.450
ruling on abortion, would be taken down by
a six to three conservative court, which is

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:18.310
what it would be if Donald Trump replaces
Ruth Bader Ginsburg with a right wing ideologue,

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:21.549
which he certainly would do if given the opportunity.

00:01:21.549 --> 00:01:28.020
Remember that Roe v. Wade is a ruling that
says states can't ban abortion altogether.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.049
Now they can almost ban it.

00:01:30.049 --> 00:01:38.130
So we've seen a whole bunch of different states
increase restrictions on any medical provider

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:44.560
that does abortions, restrict who can get
an abortion or what needs to happen in order

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:45.560
to get one.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:51.710
And sometimes these restrictions are challenged
in court and sometimes they go very high in

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.579
in the appeals process.

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:59.299
And what is ultimately left to the interpretation
of the Supreme Court when those appeals get

00:01:59.299 --> 00:02:06.889
to the court is whether they violate the spirit
of Roe v. Wade.

00:02:06.889 --> 00:02:14.130
So in practice, the way you overturn Roe v.
Wade is by change, by creating new precedent.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:21.300
A state would issue some very, very strict
ruling on abortion, and it would get appealed

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.640
all the way up to the Supreme Court.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.670
And the Supreme Court might say this is OK.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:30.500
If that were to happen, you have effectively,
by precedent undone Roe v. Wade and you would

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:36.030
have many things change in red states and
not very much would change in blue states.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:42.530
The reality is that if Roe v. Wade were effectively
overturned by Newt by creating new precedent,

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:49.270
states like Massachusetts, other blue states
are not likely to see any real changes to

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:52.840
the availability and access to safe abortions.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:55.640
The red states will get absolutely crushed.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:03:01.500
And this is another one of those ways in which
I've said before, even during the Trump presidency,

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:10.580
in blue states, we are insulated in many ways
from the destructive effect of a radical ideological,

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:14.260
reactionary presidency like that of Donald
Trump.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:21.420
So as is often the case, the destruction brought
forward by Republican policy and Right-Wing

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:25.270
Ideology will disproportionately hurt right
wingers.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:30.650
When you look at Trump trying to undo Obamacare
in Massachusetts.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:34.800
We already have something that predates Obamacare
called Romneycare.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:39.300
And it is the folks in places like Mississippi
which has one of the worst one of the worst

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.800
three health care systems in the country.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:47.110
It is those folks who are disproportionately
hurt by Donald Trump doing things like undoing

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:50.180
the individual mandate on Obamacare.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:55.090
So that's a reality that if they're able to
do it, not a lot will change in blue states.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:57.350
A lot will change in red states.

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:58.460
Now.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:02.100
Does the Republican Party really want Roe
v. Wade overturned?

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:12.010
The reason I ask is if they actually overturn
it, it's conceivable that there will be no

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:17.870
one significantly renewed enthusiasm against
Republicans at the state level in order to

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:23.360
try to legalize abortion in a lot of these
states that are likely to overturn it.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:30.520
And the reality is that since Roe v. Wade
was was issued as a decision, it has been

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:33.749
a great fundraising tool for Republicans.

00:04:33.749 --> 00:04:39.370
Republicans raise a ton of money by saying
we've got to overturn Roe v. Wade.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:44.750
We need you to vote for this person and that
person and that person from low level positions

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.340
all the way up to the president.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:51.460
We need you to do it so we can get the right
people in power to overturn Roe v. Wade if

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:53.360
they actually do it.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:59.139
They no longer have that carrot to rile up
evangelical voters.

00:04:59.139 --> 00:05:01.620
I think that there is some merit to that.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:07.860
And I question whether Republicans really
want to overturn it or whether they want to

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:12.469
keep fighting about overturning it because
it allows them to raise money.

00:05:12.469 --> 00:05:13.969
It's a question.

00:05:13.969 --> 00:05:19.770
But is Roe v. Wade in danger with a six to
three court, particularly if Donald Trump

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:21.219
gets reelected?

00:05:21.219 --> 00:05:24.120
And particularly if we maintain a Republican
Senate?

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:25.789
Yes, it is in danger.

00:05:25.789 --> 00:05:27.959
What it will mean in Massachusetts is a different
question.

